Destiny source files end in `.dd`

Destiny source files use the `.dd` extension and interface files `.ddi`, so
Destiny code is not mistaken for D. D's `.d` and `.di` files are still
accepted, so D code and packages keep working; an import finds `mod.ddi`,
`mod.dd`, `mod.di`, then `mod.d` (and the same for `package.*`).

`-H` writes `mod.ddi` for a `.dd` file and `mod.di` for a `.d` file.

Ddoc documentation source files, which used `.dd`, now use `.ddd`.
